WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.189
There is a dangerous creature that could be
anywhere in the world, hiding in plain sight,

00:00:06.189 --> 00:00:09.680
casually walking through crowded streets filled
with people.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:16.180
A monster that is nearly impossible to see,
blending into its surroundings almost perfectly.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:21.900
Not invisible, but unnoticeable, almost completely
undetectable.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.890
But then, you spot a familiar outfit in a
crowd.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.250
You now know where the creature is.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:33.239
But it goes both ways, since the moment you
find it, it knows where you are.

00:00:33.239 --> 00:00:37.960
There is now not a single place on the Earth
that you could hide where it wouldn’t find

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:38.960
you.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.219
And it won’t ever stop looking.

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:47.340
To the staff at the Foundation this creature
is known as SCP-4885.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.339
But you and I know him by a different name.

00:00:50.339 --> 00:00:56.399
You may have seen his face hundreds of times,
or stared for hours at a page trying to catch

00:00:56.399 --> 00:00:57.889
a glimpse of him.

00:00:57.889 --> 00:01:00.019
To us, he’s Waldo.

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:05.740
While this might feel like a very long-winded
and silly joke, maybe even a prank that has

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:10.420
been inserted into the SCP archives, it is
anything but.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:15.640
If you grew up any time after the elate 1980s,
then you will likely be familiar with the

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:16.670
Where’s Waldo?

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:21.869
books, but for the uninitiated, these are
a series of puzzle books created by illustrator

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:23.630
Martin Handford.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.060
Each book in the Where’s Waldo?

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.770
line contains multiple double-page spreads
of colorful, crowded scenes.

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:35.619
The goal is for readers to spot the ever-elusive
titular character, Waldo, who is hidden among

00:01:35.619 --> 00:01:37.909
the mass of other characters.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:43.189
Waldo himself is easily recognized, thanks
to a design that has become truly iconic over

00:01:43.189 --> 00:01:44.189
the years.

00:01:44.189 --> 00:01:48.859
He is always depicted as wearing a red and
while striped shirt, with a bobble hat in

00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:50.380
matching colors.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:56.130
Waldo also sports jeans, circular rimmed glasses,
and sometimes a wooden walking stick.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:03.450
So, with that important context out of the
way up front, what exactly is SCP-4885?

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:07.039
Is it the character from these children’s
books somehow brought to life?

00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:12.450
Has the character of Waldo always been a malicious,
malevolent entity, too powerful to be contained

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.810
within his own books?

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.130
Well, not exactly.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:21.250
SCP-4885 only seems to resemble the famous
children’s book character.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:26.170
Whether or not he is a living manifestation
of Waldo in the real world is both unclear

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.110
and up for debate.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:33.830
Examining its outward appearance, SCP-4885
does share the humanoid shape and looks to

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:36.730
be wearing the same recognizable clothing
of Waldo.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:42.860
There are, however, two notable bodily dissimilarities
between the Waldo on the page, and the physical

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.480
form of SCP-4885.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:50.760
For one, this Waldo appears to be much paler
to the one found in the book series.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:56.390
More noticeably however, is the fact that,
despite wearing the same circular glasses,

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:00.850
SCP-4885 seems to have no eyes.

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:06.730
Should a person learn of SCP-4885’s current
location, Waldo will simultaneously gain an

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:08.840
awareness of this person.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:15.760
Learning instantly of their victim’s location,
SCP-4885 will traverse any space necessary,

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.450
tracking their target down to anywhere they
might be in the world.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:25.100
The creature has displayed a number of space
altering abilities, including teleportation.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:31.290
SCP-4885 can also alter the state of his own
matter, allowing Waldo to phase through solid

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.370
surfaces.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:40.400
No obstacle can stop his advance: not walls,
not buildings, not even his victim’s own

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.400
body.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:46.280
When SCP-4885 finally reaches the person who
has learned of his location, Waldo will then

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:51.170
proceed to murder them in an exceptionally
excruciating manner.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:57.090
Using his matter changing abilities, he will
teleport or phase himself inside his victim,

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:01.230
pulling himself through their body and destroying
their internal organs.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:06.760
After causing catastrophic bodily damage,
SCP-4885 will then wrench their victim’s

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:11.940
jaw open, unhinging it with enough force to
climb his way out of their mouth, leaving

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:14.760
them dead, their body completely mangled.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:18.850
However, this isn’t even the final stage
of Waldo’s attack.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:25.410
There is a strange by-product left after a
fatal encounter with SCP-4885, a yellow liquid

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.810
that is produced as Waldo exits his victim’s
body.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:33.460
When this substance comes into contact with
the deceased person’s skin, it triggers

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.310
a bizarre change.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:40.510
The liquid will cause their bodies to change
after death, their skin becoming covered in

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:41.510
symbols.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:47.190
On closer inspection is becomes clear that
these symbols are illustrations, exactly like

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:50.850
the ones found in the pages of Where’s Waldo?

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:57.490
These corpses, referred to by the Foundation
as instances of SCP-4855-1, will then start

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:04.290
to act in a similar manner to SCP-4885, and
anyone who sees one or learns of its location

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.470
will cause Waldo to come looking for them.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.470
The Where’s Waldo?

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:12.970
scenes left on a deceased victim’s skin
cannot be washed off or otherwise removed

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:20.450
and the only way to undo an instance of SCP-4885-1
is to skin an infected body after death.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:22.780
However, this creates a whole new problem.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:28.270
If someone was to attempt this, in doing so
they would know the location of one of Waldo’s

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.270
victims.

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:33.590
This knowledge would mean that whomever was
trying to skin one of these bodies would themselves

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:39.290
become Waldo’s next target and would likely
end up just another instance of SCP-4885-1.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:45.260
In other words, it would be an exercise in
futility.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:49.280
Naturally, the nature of his abilities and
attack patterns makes it difficult for the

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.660
SCP Foundation to contain Waldo.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:57.680
SCP-4885 cannot be harmed through the use
of firearms, or other common, conventional

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.240
weapons at the Foundation’s disposal.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.510
You might be forgiven for thinking that making
a handful of people aware of where to find

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:08.150
Waldo at the same time would be a viable solution.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:13.210
After all, he cannot be in multiple places
at once, so perhaps he’d be unable to kill

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.610
these individuals simultaneously.

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:21.710
However, SCP-4885 has shown to be able to
cope with this approach, dispatching his victims

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:26.460
one at a time, transforming each in turn into
Where’s Waldo?

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:31.180
printed corpses, before continuing to the
next would-be victim.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:35.950
If the victim is nearby, Waldo will force
himself into their mouth, passing through

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:40.960
their body and destroying bones, organs, and
even the spinal column.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:45.480
When his victim is further away, Waldo will
phase through the nearest wall and attack

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.310
them, teleporting into his target and then
climbing out of their mouth.

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:54.550
Waldo’s location, or that of his victims’
bodies, are considered ‘infohazards’.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:59.990
Simply being aware of this information will
cause SCP-4885 to activate.

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:04.669
As a result of this, the staff at the SCP
Foundation are not even sure that Waldo is

00:07:04.669 --> 00:07:06.800
actually contained at all.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:13.980
In theory, SCP-4885 is being held at an undisclosed
Foundation site within a non-designated containment

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:19.120
chamber, since even a number on the door would
tip off what’s inside, triggering Waldo’s

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:20.120
abilities.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:24.930
But, here’s the clincher; because nobody
can know for sure where Waldo is without him

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:30.570
coming for them, nobody at the Foundation
actually knows where he’s being contained,

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:33.020
if he’s even contained at all!

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:38.120
It is worth noting that, if someone receives
a vague, non-specific description of Waldo’s

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:41.870
whereabouts, then he will make no attempt
to seek them out.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:46.900
If he is contained, and if he was to ever
breach containment, then the SCP Foundation

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:51.960
has an entire set of procedures in place to
ensure that no one ever finds Waldo.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:57.820
First, 36 containment chambers identical to
the one SCP-4885 is supposedly held in are

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:59.870
connected to a self-driving vehicle.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:04.229
An expendable D-Class personnel member is
placed into the vehicle and a random number

00:08:04.229 --> 00:08:08.120
generator will select a number from one to
36.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:12.300
The self-driving vehicle will then arrive
at the containment chamber chosen at random,

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.669
and the D-Class placed inside.

00:08:14.669 --> 00:08:19.389
Within each chamber are digital monitors,
and once the D-Class is inside a chamber,

00:08:19.389 --> 00:08:22.830
all of these monitors will display the current
location of SCP-4885.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:29.919
The Foundation has a GPS tracking device implanted
within Waldo, but this information is normally

00:08:29.919 --> 00:08:33.079
kept secret to avoid any containment breaches.

00:08:33.079 --> 00:08:38.669
The D-Class essentially acts as bait for Waldo,
forcibly given the knowledge of his location

00:08:38.669 --> 00:08:43.360
so that SCP-4885 will consider them a target.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:48.040
As part of the next phase of containment,
Foundation staff will wait, giving Waldo enough

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:52.620
time to arrive in the containment chamber
and dispatch the D-Class within.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:57.450
After this, all of the 36 containment chambers
are transported to random Foundation sites

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:03.589
in disguised trucks, so that no one is sure
where SCP-4885 ends up.

00:09:03.589 --> 00:09:10.470
Every time SCP-4885 breaches containment,
the entire procedure has to be repeated.

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:16.040
The Foundation first encountered SCP-4885
a number of years ago, inside a small wooden

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:21.209
house, the exact location of which has since
been expunged from all the SCP Foundation’s

00:09:21.209 --> 00:09:22.209
records.

00:09:22.209 --> 00:09:26.579
While on an assignment to secure an entirely
different anomaly, the Foundation’s Mobile

00:09:26.579 --> 00:09:31.980
Task Force Chi-19, also code named ‘Unrelenting
Punishment’, were the first to discover

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:32.980
Waldo.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:37.920
The three person unit consisted of Foundation
operatives named Amelia Merrick, James Klein

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:39.240
and Kurt Stoll.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:42.980
The trio cautiously entered the wooden house
where they were meant to investigate reports

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:47.629
of an anomalous, inanimate object: a pair
of black spectacles.

00:09:47.629 --> 00:09:52.019
According to initial intelligence gathered
by the SCP Foundation, these glasses were

00:09:52.019 --> 00:09:56.640
capable of killing anyone that tried to wear
them, leaving their body covered in pictures

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:59.440
like those found in a children’s book.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:00.850
Sounds familiar, doesn’t it?

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:06.740
It is unknown if these black spectacles are
the same eyewear worn by SCP-4885, but it

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:11.959
doesn’t seem like too far of a leap to assume
that this may well have been the case.

00:10:11.959 --> 00:10:16.839
Searching the ground floor, the team found
no sign of the object had been sent to recover.

00:10:16.839 --> 00:10:21.740
As Amelia, Kurt, and James made their way
upstairs, something began making scraping

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:24.879
sounds beneath them, but none of them noticed.

00:10:24.879 --> 00:10:29.730
In an abandoned bedroom on the upstairs floor
of the house, Kurt spotted a drawing on the

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:33.209
wall, which looked to have been made using
crayons.

00:10:33.209 --> 00:10:37.480
He took a photo of the illustration, and this
image is still kept in the Foundation’s

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:38.480
database.

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:44.480
It appears to be a child’s drawing, depicting
SCP-4885, wearing his signature striped shirt

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:47.980
and hat, with empty, vacant eyes.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:54.220
Next to it was scrawled one simple phrase:
“Waldo found mommy.”

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:57.920
Continuing their way through the house, the
team located the glasses they were looking

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.670
for in an upstairs bathroom.

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:04.640
However, as James bagged up the spectacles,
ready for transport back to the Foundation,

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:09.550
Kurt spotted another inscription on a nearby
wall, one that the team were certain hadn’t

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:11.399
been there when they had arrived.

00:11:11.399 --> 00:11:16.319
James stepped in to translate it using a Foundation
standard issue translation device.

00:11:16.319 --> 00:11:19.119
The phrase on the wall read “The basement.

00:11:19.119 --> 00:11:21.950
The corpses from a child’s book are in the
basement.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.829
He is there too.

00:11:23.829 --> 00:11:24.829
Fr-.”

00:11:24.829 --> 00:11:27.940
And we’re sure that you can already guess
what happened after that.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:32.939
Immediately after reading these words, James
began to groan and clutched at his stomach,

00:11:32.939 --> 00:11:35.290
showing signs of extreme pain.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:39.790
Before Amelia or Kurt had any chance to figure
out what was happening to their squadmate,

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:42.329
fingers began protruding from James’ mouth.

00:11:42.329 --> 00:11:47.579
They gripped his jaw and pulled it apart with
enough force to send his jawbone flying across

00:11:47.579 --> 00:11:49.100
the room.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:54.879
SCP-4885 climbed its way out of James’ body,
and Amelia and Kurt both opened fire on the

00:11:54.879 --> 00:11:55.920
creature.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:12:01.180
Waldo did not react, seemingly unphased by
the gunfire and sustaining no damage as he

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:05.220
approached Amelia, who would be his next victim.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:10.079
Showing his fingers into her throat, Waldo
wrenched apart Amelia’s jaw, breaking it

00:12:10.079 --> 00:12:12.749
before he clawed his way into her mouth.

00:12:12.749 --> 00:12:17.639
As he watched in horror, Kurt made a panicked
call for help to the Foundation, but it was

00:12:17.639 --> 00:12:19.310
too late.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:24.829
Waldo had already dispatched both James and
Amelia, and now Kurt was about to pay the

00:12:24.829 --> 00:12:27.170
same terrible price.

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:33.149
Ever since this incident, the Foundation believes
that they have SCP-4885 contained.

00:12:33.149 --> 00:12:37.860
When his file was created, their researchers
created an automated algorithm, designed to

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:43.569
wipe away any mention of SCP-4885’s current
location or the house he was discovered in

00:12:43.569 --> 00:12:45.559
from Foundation records.

00:12:45.559 --> 00:12:52.800
With SCP-4885 now assumed to be contained,
that only leaves one question, the same burning

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:56.060
inquiry that’s been plaguing man for decades…

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:58.230
Where’s Waldo?

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:02.660
In this case, maybe it’s safer if you don't
know.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:09.970
Now check out “The Lost SCP - SCP-000”
and “SCP-5049 - The Skin Salesman - Demon

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:15.309
Dan's Discount Homunculus Depot” for more
of the Foundation’s strangest anomalies!

